## Frontend State Management

```javascript
// core.js
let currentUser = null;           // {id, username, role, member_id}
let currentMemberId = null;       // selected member for dashboard (int or null)
let members = [];                 // all team members
let projects = [];                // all projects
let worklogData = [];             // current month's worklogs
let currentWorklogView = 'table'; // 'table' | 'calendar'

// files.js
let fileCurrentFolderId = null;   // null = root, else folder id
let fileTreeCache = [];           // nested tree from /api/files/tree
let fileListCache = [];           // current folder's files (used by delete lookup)
let fileDragDepth = 0;            // drag-enter/leave counter for overlay
```

### Key Frontend Functions
- **`api(url, opts)`** — Fetch wrapper with auto Content-Type detection
- **`isElevated()`** — Check if current user is Leader/Admin/Super_Admin
- **`canEditMember(id)`** — Permission check (elevated or own member)
- **`toast(msg, type)`** — Show notification (`type = 'error'` | `'success'`)
- **`esc(s)`** — HTML-escape strings (prevent XSS)

---

## Permission Model

### Decorators in Flask
```python
@login_required       # Any authenticated user
@elevated_required    # Admin, Leader, or Super_Ultimate_ADMIN
@admin_required       # Super_Ultimate_ADMIN only
```

### Frontend Checks
```javascript
if (!isElevated()) { /* show error, return */ }  // For elevated routes

if (currentUser.id !== member_id && !isElevated()) {  // For own-member checks
    toast('Permission denied', 'error');
    return;
}
```

### File Share Permission Rules
| Action | Who can do it |
|--------|---------------|
| List tree / view folder contents | Any logged-in user |
| Create folder | Any logged-in user |
| Rename folder | Creator OR elevated |
| Delete folder (must be empty) | Creator OR elevated |
| Upload file | Any logged-in user |
| Download file | Any logged-in user |
| Delete file | Uploader OR elevated |
| View storage stats | Any logged-in user |

Enforcement lives in `app/files.py` — each mutating route checks `currentUser.id == row.created_by/uploaded_by` OR `role in ELEVATED_ROLES`.

